-power cost <γ_j2^(−k−1); the total additional cost is <γ_j. Leave positive-diameter members and empty members unchanged. The resulting cover has all nonempty diameters d_i positive, d_i≤r_j, and q-cost <2γ_j. For each i partition [0,1] into N_i=⌈1/d_i⌉ closed intervals of length 1/N_i≤d_i; since d_i≤1, N_i≤1/d_i+1≤2/d_i. The products U_i×K_iℓ cover F, have diameter ≤√2d_i, and form a countable family (a countable union of finite families), which can be enumerated by ℕ with empty sets appended. Their total (q+1)-cost is at most 2(√2)^(q+1)∑d_i^q<4(√2)^(q+1)γ_j, and their diameters are ≤√2r_j→0. For any fixed δ>0, all sufficiently large j have √2r_j≤δ; these product families are then admissible Nat-indexed δ-covers, so C_(q+1)(F,δ)≤4(√2)^(q+1)γ_j for all such j. Letting j→∞ gives C_(q+1)(F,δ)=0. This holds for every δ>0; the exact M008 supremum formula gives H^(q+1)(F)=0. M012 at NNReal exponent q+1 gives dim_H(F)≤q+1. Since this holds for every q>D, density gives dim_H(F)≤D+1. For n=0, F is isometric to [0,1]; interval covers of mesh h have at most 1/h+1 members of diameter ≤h, whose total a-cost tends to zero for every a>1. The same M008 scale formula and M012 give dim_H(F)≤1=D+1. Isometries preserve ediam, cover conditions and the exact M008 formula.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/11/declaration\",\"value\":\"Set η_i=ε·2^(−i−1)/(1+ρ_i^s), interpreted using the underlying real value of the finite diameter ρ_i; thus η_i>0 and η_iρ_i^s≤ε·2^(−i−1).\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/12/declaration\",\"value\":\"For each i, if B_i is nonempty, choose an open interval J_i containing B_i whose length is at most diam(B_i)+η_i≤ρ_i+η_i, by enlarging its infimum/supremum enclosure by total width η_i. If B_i is empty, choose any open interval of length η_i; it contains B_i and satisfies the same bound.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/objects\",\"value\":[\"E\",\"F\",\"D\",\"I\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"V_i\",\"ρ_i\",\"A_i\",\"B_i\",\"J_i\",\"η_i\",\"ε\",\"c_s\",\"ν\"]},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"ν\",\"type\":\"finite measure volume.restrict([0,1]) on ℝ\",\"scope\":\"R001/S002\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define ν=volume.restrict([0,1]) on the ambient Borel measurable space ℝ; by the restriction definition and M011, ν(ℝ)=volume([0,1])=1.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"M011\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"volume\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/applications/-\",\"value\":{\"input\":\"M001\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"id\":\"A001\",\"bindings\":\"Instantiate again with X=the product ambient Euclidean space, set F, and NNReal exponent d the coercion of s+1.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"The product ambient space carries its extended metric, Borel measurable structure; the result H^(s+1)(F)=⊤ was established immediately before this use.\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/applications/-\",\"value\":{\"input\":\"M011\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"id\":\"A011\",\"bindings\":\"Instantiate at the fixed real endpoints 0 and 1 to compute volume([0,1]) for the total mass of ν.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[]}}]}}","status":"completed"}}

